  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nThe cold front will move southeast of our area this morning with \nhigh pressure building into the region behind it. This will lead to \ndry and somewhat cooler conditions as we head into the weekend. Highs\ntoday will range from the mid 60s north to the lower 70s in the \nsouth, with highs on Saturday mainly in the 65 to 70 degree range. \n\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2) \nA mid level short wave will move out of the mid Mississippi Valley \nSaturday night and across the Ohio Valley Sunday into Sunday night. \nThere remains some uncertainty as to how much moisture will be \npulled up into our area ahead of this, with the NAM and GFS still the\nmost bullish. However, the ECMWF/ECMWF mean have trended just a bit \nwetter, so will continue with chance pops. \n\nA deeper mid/upper level trough is forecast to progress east across \nthe central CONUS early next week, but there remains significant \ndifferences in the timing of this as well as the timing/placement/ \nstrength of any embedded short waves. As a result, a fair bit of \nuncertainty continues with the forecast through the second half of \nthe long term period so will still broad brush with chance pops.",
